# 34_gateway_obe.ledc — Gateway / Out-of-Body Threshold (Monroe septon bed), ~32 min
# ALTERED STATE: the Monroe "Focus 10" mind-awake / body-asleep threshold used as a launch point
#   for out-of-body and expanded-awareness experiences. Scaffolding for the practice, not a
#   guarantee of any state. Arc: alpha 10 induction -> glide to theta 4 Hz (Focus-10) -> deep
#   multi-carrier hold (16 min) -> gentle return to alpha.
#
# V2 FEATURES USED (and why):
#   * SEPTON multi-carrier STACK (Monroe US 5,356,368) — the 4 Hz theta beat is delivered by
#     THREE stacked binaural pairs (200/204, 208/212, plus the primary 265->271 / 275) sharing one
#     4 Hz delta-f. This produces cross-ear binaural AND within-ear monaural beats at once: a
#     richer, more robust FFR than a single pair (playbook A5, monroe_patents_guide.md 4b).
#   * EEG-CONTOUR carrier, wave 7 (Monroe US 5,213,562) — one layer uses the non-sinusoidal
#     EEG-contour carrier shape ("neither sinusoidal, nor square, nor triangular"), 250/254 => a
#     4 Hz beat from the L/R detune. The patent claims the contour itself aids entrainment
#     (monroe_patents_guide.md 4c).
#   * TRAPEZOID isochronic pulse, audio env=3 + duty + attack — a crisp 4 Hz body-buzz drum
#     (137 Hz, 40% duty, 5 ms click-safe edge) adds a felt isochronic pulse to the smooth beats
#     (playbook A2).
#   * PHASED PINK BED with rotating pan (~-100:100 over 6 s) — Monroe's "Phased Pink Sound",
#     panned L<->R on a ~6 s cycle, held ~-20 dB under the beats; claimed +30% FFR
#     (monroe_patents_guide.md 4a).
#   * Audio beat JITTER (0.3 Hz over 53 s, a non-commensurate period) on the primary binaural —
#     anti-acclimatization wander of the 4 Hz beat (playbook A3).
#
# RESEARCH / PATENT CITATION:
#   Monroe Focus-levels / septon / phased-pink / EEG-contour: reports/session_research/
#   monroe_patents_guide.md (US 5,213,562, US 5,356,368) and monroe_focus_levels_map.md. All four
#   Monroe patents are EXPIRED (patent_landscape_ave.md) -> free prior art. "Hemi-Sync" is a
#   trademark and is deliberately NOT used.
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of photic
#   migraine. Do not use while driving or operating machinery. Stop if you feel dizzy or unwell.
#   EXPERIENTIAL, not medical. Every LED rate is <=10 Hz (below the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band);
#   warm amber sine flicker, brightness dim (<=22%), ramps in 15 s / out over the return; audio
#   fades in 60 s. Headphones recommended (binaural). Lie down, eyes closed. Engine note: AM depth
#   is fixed (~0.1) in this build, so the trapezoid drum is a gentle buzz, not a hard on/off.
#
# Duration: ~32 min.  LED cols: time freq duty bright R G B mask env phase attack
#   Audio: A time freq pan vol mod [ch] [freqR] [wave] [duty] [env] [phase] [attack] [jitter]
#   (wave 7 = EEG-contour carrier; env 3 = trapezoid gate).
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the > prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Phased pink bed (runs throughout, fades in first) ---
A 0 220 ~-100:100:6000 >0 0 6 0 5             # ch6 phased PINK bed: L<->R pan on 6 s cycle; vol fade-in
A 90000 220 ~-100:100:6000 30 0 6 0 5         # ch6 pink settled 15 (~-20 dB bed)

# --- Induction / alpha 10 Hz (00:00-02:00): primary binaural + amber light fade in ---
0 10 50 >0 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # amber 10 Hz sine flicker (mask 15); bright fade-in
A 0 265 0 >0 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000     # ch1 PRIMARY binaural: carrier 265 / freqR 275 => 10 Hz; beat jitter 0.3 Hz/53 s
S 3000 default 20 "Lie back, body heavy and still. We begin at ten hertz, letting the body settle toward sleep while the mind stays awake."
15000 10 50 22 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # brightness reaches 22% (>=10 s ramp-in)
A 120000 >265 0 90 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000  # vol settled 45; carrier begins the descent ramp 265->271 (beat 10->4)

# --- Deepen (02:00-12:00): glide alpha 10 -> theta 4 Hz (Focus 10, ~0.6 Hz/min) ---
120000 >10 50 22 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # LED flicker tracks the beat 10->4
S 120000 default 20 "Down and inward. The body sleeps; you remain aware. Approaching the threshold."

# --- FOCUS-10 HOLD (12:00-28:00 = 16 min): septon stack + EEG-contour + trapezoid drum ---
A 720000 271 0 100 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000   # ch1 primary at 4 Hz beat, fuller vol; jitter on
720000 4 50 ~14:26:12000 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # LED 4 Hz sine field, 0.1 Hz brightness breath
A 720000 200 0 >0 0 2 204 0                   # ch2 SEPTON pair 200/204 => 4 Hz; fade in
A 780000 200 0 50 0 2 204 0                   # ch2 settled 25 (secondary layer)
A 720000 208 0 >0 0 3 212 0                   # ch3 SEPTON pair 208/212 => 4 Hz; fade in
A 780000 208 0 44 0 3 212 0                   # ch3 settled 22
A 720000 250 0 >0 0 4 254 7                   # ch4 EEG-CONTOUR carrier (wave 7) 250/254 => 4 Hz; fade in
A 780000 250 0 40 0 4 254 7                   # ch4 settled 20 (contour-shaped layer)
A 720000 137 0 >0 4 5 0 0 40 3 0 5            # ch5 TRAPEZOID iso drum: 137 Hz, 4 Hz gate, 40% duty, 5 ms edge; fade in
A 780000 137 0 60 4 5 0 0 40 3 0 5            # ch5 drum settled 30
S 720000 default 20 "You are at the threshold now. Rest in the hum, poised and clear. Let a smooth intention to lift and float form gently."
S 1200000 default 20 "Steady here. If sensations of movement or floating arise, stay calm and simply observe them."

# --- Return (28:00-31:00): septon/EEG/drum fade, beat 4 -> alpha 10 ---
A 1680000 200 0 >50 0 2 204 0                 # ch2 fade
A 1860000 200 0 0 0 2 204 0
A 1680000 208 0 >44 0 3 212 0                 # ch3 fade
A 1860000 208 0 0 0 3 212 0
A 1680000 250 0 >40 0 4 254 7                 # ch4 EEG-contour fade
A 1860000 250 0 0 0 4 254 7
A 1680000 137 0 >60 4 5 0 0 40 3 0 5          # ch5 trapezoid drum fade
A 1860000 137 0 0 4 5 0 0 40 3 0 5
A 1680000 >271 0 100 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000  # ch1 carrier ramps 271->265 (beat 4->10)
1680000 >4 50 22 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # LED 4->10 lockstep (drop breath LFO)
S 1680000 default 20 "Gently returning. Let the body wake with you, carrying the stillness of the threshold home."

# --- Soft close (31:00-32:00): primary + pink + light fade to 0 ---
A 1860000 265 0 >100 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000  # beat back at alpha 10; vol fade 50->0
1860000 10 50 >22 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # brightness fade 22->0
A 1860000 220 ~-100:100:6000 >30 0 6 0 5      # phased pink fade 15->0
A 1920000 265 0 0 0 1 275 0 50 4 0 3 0.3:53000    # end: ch1 vol 0
1920000 10 50 0 220 120 0 15 1 0 3   # end: brightness 0
A 1920000 220 ~-100:100:6000 0 0 6 0 5        # end: pink vol 0

S 1920000 default 20 "WAKE UP!"
S 1930000 default 40 "WAKE UP!"
S 1940000 default 50 "WAKE UP!"
S 1950000 default 60 "WAKE UP!"
